    <string name="swipe_learn_more">Like HeliBoard, Chirp can use a compatible gesture library that you add yourself, usually Google\'s libjni_latinimegoogle.so taken from a Google Apps (GApps) package. Chirp never downloads or includes it. Using it is your choice and is subject to that library\'s own licence.\n\nThis phone needs the %1$s version. Chirp checks the file\'s SHA-256 against the known release and warns about anything else. A library not built for 16 KB memory pages may fail to load on Android 15+ phones that use them. The library runs inside Chirp with Chirp\'s permissions, including network access, so use only a file from a source you trust.</string>
